# Silicon Labs Project Configuration Tools: slcp, v0, Component selection file.
project_name: aiml_soc_voice_control_light_blink_concurrent_efr32_micriumos
label: aiml_soc_voice_control_light_blink_concurrent_efr32_micriumos
description: |
  This application uses a keyword spotting model to detect the spoken words "on" and "off" from microphone audio in a MicriumOS kernel task. When "on" is detected, a sine blink model drives LED0 with PWM for three cycles, then leaves the LED on. The concurrent load variant keeps both models initialized in RAM so the blink model is available without swapping model memory.
category: AI/ML Application
filter:
- name: Capability
  value:
  - Machine Learning
- name: Device Type
  value:
  - SoC
- name: MCU
  value:
  - 32-bit MCU
- name: Project Difficulty
  value:
  - Advanced
package: aiml_app
quality: experimental
